    "field": "Global flood risk assessment",
    "problem": "Analyses of future flood risk have been based on relatively few climate models, making it difficult to robustly quantify the associated uncertainties in projections and assess consistency across different generations of models.",
    "method": "Future global flood exposure is projected by simulating river discharge from CMIP5 and CMIP6 climate models, fitting an extreme value distribution to determine flood frequency, and linking the resulting inundation area to a global population dataset to quantify potentially exposed populations.",
    "task": "The task is to project future global flood exposure by comparing new CMIP6 climate model projections with the previous CMIP5 generation and investigating the associated model uncertainties.",
